# Copy to config/mcp-env/users.csv (gitignored) and edit. Read by
# scripts/70-users.sh, which creates each user in CML and gives every
# non-admin user access to every lab on the controller, then writes the
# generated passwords to config/mcp-env/users-credentials.csv.
#
# email is the CML username: a person logs in to CML with the same
# address the Cloudflare Access policy checks. role is admin or user.
# Admins see every lab already, so only users get the lab grant. Rerun
# the script after importing a new lab to grant it to everyone.
#
# The email must be 32 characters or fewer, which every Cisco CEC
# address is. Synthetic class: scripts/70-users.sh class netsec 10 cisco.com
email,fullname,role
jdoe@example.com,Jane Doe,admin
astudent@example.com,A Student,user
bstudent@example.com,B Student,user
